cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below. Not peer reviewed. Produced by AI models under the direction of the repository owner (see AI_DISCLOSURE.md)."
title: "The pentagonal bipyramid as the unique logarithmic-energy minimiser for seven points on the sphere: a Lean 4 warrant (Conjecture 1 of Armentano et al.)"
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23086382"
authors:
  - name: alejandrozarco
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandrozarco/thomson-n7-log"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalisation states and checks that, among all configurations of seven distinct points on the unit
  sphere S^2, the regular pentagonal bipyramid uniquely minimises the logarithmic energy, up to orthogonal
  transformations and relabelling (Conjecture 1 of Armentano et al., J. Symbolic Comput. 137 (2026)); Comparator and
  the independent checker nanoda accept it. The same is stated and checked for the Riesz s = 2 energy. AI-produced,
  not peer reviewed. The repository also contains the exact certificates with independent checkers.
keywords:
  - Thomson problem
  - logarithmic energy
  - Riesz energy
  - pentagonal bipyramid
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Lean 4
license: Apache-2.0
